S3 Bucket in AWS DevOps - Simple Explanation

Amazon S3 (Simple Storage Service) is used to store files in the cloud.

In DevOps, S3 is commonly used for:
1. Store Application Files
Example:
index.html
style.css
Images
Build artifacts (.jar, .war, .zip)

After Jenkins builds your application, it can upload the files to an S3 bucket.

2. Static Website Hosting
In your StarWeb project, instead of running Nginx on EC2, you can upload:
index.html
style.css

to an S3 bucket and AWS serves the website directly.

3. Terraform Remote State Storage
When using Terraform:

terraform.tfstate
